# The finish of norm_upper_1 (milestone2.md, "When something is not finite"): the largest magnitude
# when no element was a NaN (the mask ok) and it is finite, with the flag true; otherwise the
# canonical NaN and the flag false. An infinite element made m infinite.
kernel:        norm_finish_1
input:         m
input:         mask ok
output:        r
output:        mask flag
value:         m
ensures:       finite_or_nan r flag=flag if=ok
min_precision: 1
source:        the finish of a fold of maxima: the maximum or the canonical NaN (milestone2.md)
license:       proof: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
cone_exempt:   the outputs are selects after the mask ok and an explicit test that the maximum is finite (fold_finish_1), which is what the kernel claims

t         = select(ok, m, const nan)
(r, flag) = fold_finish_1(t)
